{:edb/db-before-t 2387 :edb/db-after-t 2388 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535700 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:31:17.814Z" 13194139535700 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362107 13194139535700 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362121 13194139535700 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362128 13194139535700 true] [17592186157211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362114 13194139535700 true] [17592186157708 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535700 true] [17592186157708 1100 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B = {\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}}$ of $R^{2}$, find $[x]_{B}$ if $x = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535700 false] [17592186157708 1100 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535700 true] [17592186157708 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362107 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362108 13194139535700 true] [17592186362107 1089 "q-102341" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362107 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535700 true] [17592186362107 1100 "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $4{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362107 1113 #uuid "ff9815f5-68cc-5b46-8c06-f6cff798eab0" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362107 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot (-5)+(-12)\\cdot 4}{(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-75-48}{25+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{123}{41} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}=4\\cdot (-3)=-12.\n$$" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362109 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362110 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362111 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362112 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362113 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1041 "selection" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362113 13194139535700 true] [17592186362108 1110 #uuid "23a77b6e-39ae-5cd9-9613-760704a65107" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362109 1034 "-8" 13194139535700 true] [17592186362109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535700 true] [17592186362109 1111 #uuid "705a0be6-2679-5da0-9c97-3725575859e7"